{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK854LEidqmwiL5FTAhS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`STATIC_URL` and `MEDIA_URL` now pick up the request's `SCRIPT_NAME` prefix when they're set as relative paths. Because the fix is in the settings object itself, `{% static %}`, `StaticFilesStorage` and `FileSystemStorage` all get the prefix without any changes to the tag or the storage classes.\n\n**What changed in `django/conf/__init__.py`:** a new `LazySettings._add_script_prefix()` is applied when either setting is read, and the result is cached like any other setting.\n- **Relative path** (e.g. `static/`): gets the script prefix in front, so it becomes `/subpath/static/`.\n- **Full URL** (e.g. `https://cdn.example.com/static/`) or **path starting with `/`**: returned unchanged, so existing setups behave as before.\n\nI also added two lines to `docs/releases/3.1.txt`.\n\n**Tests:** I ran `settings_tests`, `staticfiles_tests`, `file_storage` and `template_tests.syntax_tests.test_static`.\n- **4 failures, all `test_setting_changed` in `file_storage`:** these tests set `MEDIA_URL` to the relative `overridden_media_url/` and now get `/overridden_media_url/` back. That's the new behaviour doing what it should; the tests' expected value would need updating, which the rules don't allow me to do.\n- **2 errors (`StaticLiveServerView`, `FileLikeObjectTestCase`):** `PermissionError` while setting up, which looks like this sandbox blocking network sockets rather than the change.\n\n**One limitation:** the prefixed value is cached the first time it's read. If different requests in the same process use different `SCRIPT_NAME` values, the first one sticks; this matches how upstream Django handles it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":22598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0